# Global instructions (codex)

Machine-local: copied to `other/codex/AGENTS.md` by `bin/seed_other.sh` and
linked to `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` by `bin/symlink_files.sh`. Codex has no rules
directory, so anything that would be a `dots/claude/rules/*.md` file for
Claude Code goes here by hand — keep it short, and keep private details out of
the repo by editing the real file, never this template.

## Python

- Run Python tooling through `uv run` (`uv run python`, `uv run pytest`,
  `uv run ruff`) so it resolves to the project's virtualenv.

## tmux

- The default tmux server hosts every live agent session on this machine.
  Never run `kill-server`, `kill-session`, `source-file`, or `set-hook`
  against it. Tests that need a server must pass a throwaway socket
  (`tmux -L <name> ...`) spelled out in the command itself.

## Worktrees

- Anchor every command at the worktree you are working in (`git -C <path>`,
  absolute paths, or `cd <path> && ...` in one command). A shell's cwd does
  not survive between steps.

## Workspace knowledge

- Cross-repo knowledge (architecture, repo relationships, where infra,
  monitors and secrets live, runbooks, external systems) lives in the wikillm
  vault at `~/dev/wiki`. For questions about the wider system rather than the
  current repo's own code, consult it BEFORE grepping across repos: start at
  `~/dev/wiki/wiki/_index/INDEX.md`, read the 1-3 relevant pages, follow
  `[[wikilinks]]` lazily. `$WORKSPACE` in wiki pages means `~/dev`.
- Trust rules: check `confidence` and `last_verified` frontmatter. Unverified
  imports are leads, not gospel; verify against the repo or live system before
  acting, then stamp `last_verified` on the page.
- Write back: when you learn or verify something cross-repo, capture it in the
  wiki per its SCHEMA.md (edit or create the page, update `wiki/_index/`
  INDEX and LOG, commit). Knowledge that stays only in a session dies with it.
